Tokenomics — Documentation‑Driven Value Ecosystem
Note: This is an evolving, living ecosystem of protection, where every component develops and adapts in real time.

VaultForge‑Live introduces a new category of tokenomics built on authorship, continuity, and innovation evolution, rather than speculation or financial trading.
This system operates through a dual‑unit documentation model that reflects how the world interacts with your work and how legitimate access is established.

Relics — Authored Innovation Units
Relics represent timestamped innovation, public‑safe disclosures, and the evolving authorship timeline.
They form the foundation of the VaultForge‑Live value layer by documenting the creation and evolution of your work.

Shadow Units™ — Interaction Documentation
Shadow Units™ are generated automatically when the public vault is interacted with (such as cloning, viewing, or derivative referencing).
They serve as continuity markers, interaction records, and authorship‑preservation artifacts, strengthening the evidentiary timeline of the ecosystem.
These units do not assign guilt or make legal claims; they simply document how the system is accessed.

Light Units™ — Legitimate Access Documentation
Light Units™ represent the documentation of legitimate alignment with the system.
They appear when users or organizations engage with your work under proper usage terms, reflecting authorized participation and continuity.

Creation Tokens — Authored Value Layer
Creation Tokens (minted through private‑vault logic) represent the innovation‑side value of the ecosystem.
They are tied to relics and reflect the growth, evolution, and authorship of the VaultForge‑Live environment.

